  "title": "Data Persistence & Rotation Lifecycle",
  "kind": "state_lifecycle",
  "purpose": "Focus on the store.py persistence hub and its interactions with service.py (write path), config.py (rotation threshold, state dir), hooks.py (post-store trigger), and modes.json (note attribution). Shows how notes are written with fsync, how rotation is triggered by file size, and how journal read-back works. Answers: how are thinking notes stored, rotated, and retrieved?",
